WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:07.890
On May 12, 2588, the entity known as SCP-UBU
manifested in Kangaatsiaq, Greenland, like

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:11.400
something out of the most nightmarish Kaiju
movie never made.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:16.240
Soon after, there was no more death, but the
world was filled with such chaos and despair

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:19.760
that humanity longed for that eternal release.

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:25.050
From its enormous stomping feet to its cloaca,
to its face, featureless save for a gaping,

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:30.460
grinning, devouring mouth, the entity was
pure malice with all the time in the world.

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:36.829
UBU decimated the planet, breaking the spirit
of mankind and razing every city to the ground.

00:00:36.829 --> 00:00:41.250
In the earlier days of UBU's invasion, when
there was still dry land, and people still

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:45.750
wanted to talk to each other rather than joining
floating islands of eternal, chemically-induced

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:50.280
slumber, they would commiserate about the
shared misery of the state of things.

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:51.360
"Oh, UBU?

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:55.520
My daughter hasn't spoken to me ever since
that monster shoved my whole body down her

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:56.520
throat…"

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:57.520
Someone would say.

00:00:57.520 --> 00:01:02.220
Another would pipe up, trying to one-up the
first man in a sort of trauma Olympics: "Didn't

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:03.420
you see me in the news?

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:07.850
UBU carried me around for a week, snacking
on me every now and then — like I was his

00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:08.850
personal turkey leg.

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:10.650
It was hell — but honestly?

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:13.600
Part of me felt a little bummed out when he
threw me away…"

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:18.380
Yet another person would chime in, like veterans
swapping war stories over a drink at the bar,

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:22.620
"UBU made me eat a pair of my pants, whole
thing, zipper and all.

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:27.400
Then he decided he thought that was funny,
made me eat pair after pair after pair of

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:28.470
'em, rinse, repeat.

00:01:28.470 --> 00:01:33.120
By the time he got bored, I had eaten probably
around 20 pairs, sort of got a taste for them

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:34.120
after that…"

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:40.149
Everyone on the planet had good reason to
despise SCP-UBU, but no one held more hate

00:01:40.149 --> 00:01:44.520
in his heart for the pale, wicked creature
than Dr. Laurence Michaud.

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:49.790
Before the world was turned upside down (sometimes
literally), Dr. Michaud was a member of the

00:01:49.790 --> 00:01:53.420
mysterious O5 council at the SCP Foundation.

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:56.500
To be specific, he was O5-11.

00:01:56.500 --> 00:02:00.920
But that prestigious position at the Foundation
couldn't protect him or his loved ones from

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:02.390
the wrath of UBU.

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:06.790
When Dr. Michaud was off duty, UBU attacked
him and his wife.

00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:09.869
First, it impaled his wife on a broom handle.

00:02:09.869 --> 00:02:13.780
Next, it threw Dr. Michaud into an open pool
of sewage in the street.

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:18.771
Then, it bathed him in the filthy water, using
his screaming wife as a scrubbing brush, all

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:22.769
the while whistling a horrible little bathtub
song.

00:02:22.769 --> 00:02:26.570
Centuries after that awful experience, as
Dr. Michaud watched most of his colleagues

00:02:26.570 --> 00:02:31.030
give up and choose the closest thing to death
in this broken world, he became even more

00:02:31.030 --> 00:02:33.420
determined to do something about it.

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:39.681
On January 14, 3030, Dr. Michaud abandoned
the SCPS Naismith, and his fellow O5 council

00:02:39.681 --> 00:02:45.319
members in search of the SCPS Concrake, an
abandoned craft to the Southeast.

00:02:45.319 --> 00:02:49.950
It wasn't an easy journey, rowing all the
way there in a lifeboat, never knowing when

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:55.250
the great white beast would emerge from the
water and choose him as its next unfortunate

00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:56.260
plaything.

00:02:56.260 --> 00:03:00.380
He could see the SCPS Concrake, still floating
there, untouched.

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:05.849
But before he could row any closer, something
collided with the lifeboat from below, snapping

00:03:05.849 --> 00:03:07.010
it in half.

00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:11.000
Dr. Michaud's stomach dropped at the sight
of pale flesh, but it was soon replaced with

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:16.730
relief when he saw that the thing that had
broken his lifeboat was not, in fact, UBU.

00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:21.120
It was an injured narwhal, behaving erratically
due to its wounds.

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:23.790
The culprit was almost certainly UBU.

00:03:23.790 --> 00:03:28.620
It wasn't content to just torment humans,
but instead must have been targeting any life

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:30.900
form that could feel pain and fear.

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:35.540
In his own words, Dr. Michaud had put it:
"At least a mass extinction wouldn't have

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:37.230
made it that personal."

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:42.770
After the lifeboat broke apart, Michaud swam
to the Corncrake, exhaustion and cold straining

00:03:42.770 --> 00:03:43.849
his muscles.

00:03:43.849 --> 00:03:49.330
It took him two hours to reach the abandoned
cargo barge and containment site, but eventually,

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:52.330
he managed to climb up over the side and get
on board.

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:56.790
There was one very special thing about the
Corncrake, the thing that made it worth crossing

00:03:56.790 --> 00:04:00.159
the ocean in a fragile little lifeboat to
find.

00:04:00.159 --> 00:04:04.579
Every anomaly that made the Ganymede list,
the list of anomalies considered too dangerous

00:04:04.579 --> 00:04:10.310
to abandon even in an apocalyptic scenario,
was contained on the Corncrake.

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:15.030
If there was anything left that the Foundation,
or anyone else, hadn't tried to use to defeat

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:18.100
UBU, it would be on that ship.

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:22.600
After taking a little while to recover, Dr.
Michaud embarked on an initial exploration

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:23.750
of the craft.

00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:26.540
All the staff were gone, as he had expected.

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:31.949
Thankfully, he still had his O5 ID card, and
it still worked like a charm, unlocking all

00:04:31.949 --> 00:04:34.320
of the automated security systems onboard.

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:38.570
A lot of what he found was in ruins, but some
things had survived.

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:43.790
He found ten Hominid Replicators from SCP-2000,
in perfect working order.

00:04:43.790 --> 00:04:50.729
There was a cage containing the remains of
SCP-2845, The Deer, though UBU had done significant

00:04:50.729 --> 00:04:52.400
damage to it.

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:58.330
SCP-319, A Curious Device, was there, contained
in a space-locked vacuum chamber.

00:04:58.330 --> 00:05:02.039
This one was notable for its potential ability
to destroy the universe.

00:05:02.039 --> 00:05:08.830
He found a couple of Safe-class anomalies,
such as SCP-YEZ, "Crowd Control for the Practical

00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:12.530
Optimist," and SCP-FNA, the "Portable Warehouse."

00:05:12.530 --> 00:05:16.250
The latter of the two was a portable door
frame to a pocket dimension.

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:22.690
He also stumbled across SCP-001, Last Ride
of the Day, an old Prometheus Labs prototype

00:05:22.690 --> 00:05:24.440
of a time machine.

00:05:24.440 --> 00:05:29.610
And possibly most importantly, he found SCP-076.

00:05:29.610 --> 00:05:32.970
The coffin was open, but Able didn't attack
Dr. Michaud.

00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:38.150
He wasn't consumed with murderous rage and
bloodlust, the way he always was before.

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:43.200
Instead, he was just sitting on the edge of
the ship, silently staring at the sea.

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:47.090
When he spotted Michaud, he gave him a small
wave, and did nothing else.

00:05:47.090 --> 00:05:51.750
The centuries of a world without death, a
world without killing, without victory in

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:54.340
battle, had taken its toll on him.

00:05:54.340 --> 00:05:59.500
For possibly the first time in his eternal
life, Able was depressed.

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:04.880
Nine days after he first inspected the Concrake,
Michaud began to formulate a plan.

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:09.919
He loaded all of the hominid receptors into
SCP-FNA, using a thankfully still-working

00:06:09.919 --> 00:06:10.919
forklift.

00:06:10.919 --> 00:06:16.240
Next, he was able to unseal the sealed portion
of SCP-001, Last Ride of the Day, and get

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:19.030
his hands on the details of the anomaly.

00:06:19.030 --> 00:06:25.720
It read: "SCP-001 is capable of temporally
relocating to its relative position 15,000

00:06:25.720 --> 00:06:27.860
years prior to activation.

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:34.160
This temporal displacement is divergent/paradox-irrelevant;
in other words, a separate timeline is created

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:35.810
as a landing point.

00:06:35.810 --> 00:06:40.069
For example, if an occupant from timeline
x were to murder their parents in utero in

00:06:40.069 --> 00:06:46.060
timeline y, the y iteration of the occupant
would no longer exist, but the occupant themselves,

00:06:46.060 --> 00:06:48.070
being from x, would be unharmed.

00:06:48.070 --> 00:06:55.130
When in a fully active state, SCP-001 deploys
a five-meter-high telescopic antenna that

00:06:55.130 --> 00:06:57.720
functions as a Koloko wave energy sink."

00:06:57.720 --> 00:07:03.180
Essentially, Koloko waves could only be produced
as a byproduct of the Universe suddenly being

00:07:03.180 --> 00:07:08.919
exterminated, and ZK-class reality failures
produce the most Koloko waves.

00:07:08.919 --> 00:07:13.889
In one of these scenarios, SCP-001 would be
able to use these waves to go back in time

00:07:13.889 --> 00:07:21.040
15,000 years, effectively resetting reality
to a point far before that catastrophe happened.

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:26.510
This information allowed him to put his plan
together, to resurrect Project Beluga.

00:07:26.510 --> 00:07:30.389
Step one, plant explosive charges around SCP-319.

00:07:30.389 --> 00:07:36.979
Step two, hide anything potentially useful
against SCP-UBU inside of SCP-FNA.

00:07:36.979 --> 00:07:40.910
Step three, get into the cockpit with SCP-FNA
in tow.

00:07:40.910 --> 00:07:43.220
Step four, raise the Koloko sink.

00:07:43.220 --> 00:07:47.200
And step five...blow the whole thing up.

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:50.419
Three days later, it was time to put the plan
into motion.

00:07:50.419 --> 00:07:54.570
Dr. Michaud placed the charges around SCP-319's
vacuum chamber.

00:07:54.570 --> 00:07:57.950
There was enough in place to implode the walls
of the vacuum chamber.

00:07:57.950 --> 00:08:00.849
He closed the bulkhead and began deploying
the Koloko sink.

00:08:00.849 --> 00:08:01.849
10 percent...25 percent...30 percent...

00:08:01.849 --> 00:08:07.000
Suddenly, he could hear a loud crashing sound.

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:08.390
The ship began to tilt.

00:08:08.390 --> 00:08:09.390
Oh no...

00:08:09.390 --> 00:08:11.140
He could hear the distant sound of menacing
giggles.

00:08:11.140 --> 00:08:17.580
The sink reached 45%, 57%, but as UBU grew
closer, he quickly overrode the system to

00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:19.129
lower the sink.

00:08:19.129 --> 00:08:23.409
45%, 30%, 25%, 10%.

00:08:23.409 --> 00:08:28.539
UBU grew closer and closer, and as it approached,
it began to whistle the tune it once used

00:08:28.539 --> 00:08:31.430
when it "bathed" Michaud and his wife in the
sewer.

00:08:31.430 --> 00:08:36.260
UBU began to pound against the blast door,
becoming increasingly frustrated as it struggled

00:08:36.260 --> 00:08:37.469
to break through.

00:08:37.469 --> 00:08:41.710
Suddenly, another voice cut through the air,
an unexpected one.

00:08:41.710 --> 00:08:47.440
SCP-076, Able, called out to Michaud, encouraging
him to carry on while Able held the beast

00:08:47.440 --> 00:08:48.440
back.

00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:53.390
As Able and UBU engaged in an epic battle,
Michaud suddenly remembered something: there

00:08:53.390 --> 00:08:56.190
was an express deployment module for the Koloko
sink.

00:08:56.190 --> 00:08:58.880
With no time to waste, he activated it.

00:08:58.880 --> 00:09:01.140
All at once, he hit the detonator.

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:07.140
And then...the year was 11,970, and the date
was February 14.

00:09:07.140 --> 00:09:13.829
13,963 years later, the SCP Foundation discovered
something beneath a mound of earth and snow

00:09:13.829 --> 00:09:16.920
near the northern border of Lapland, Finland.

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:21.709
It was a shipping container with a reinforced
exterior, the interior of which could only

00:09:21.709 --> 00:09:25.030
be accessed through a fortified bulkhead on
one side.

00:09:25.030 --> 00:09:29.560
The words SCP-001 were written on the side
in black paint.

00:09:29.560 --> 00:09:33.209
In spite of this, the object was given the
designation SCP-8048.

00:09:33.209 --> 00:09:38.649
A narrow, winding tunnel through the mound
of earth and snow was discovered, leading

00:09:38.649 --> 00:09:40.660
from the door to the outside world.

00:09:40.660 --> 00:09:45.670
The tunnel had significant wear, clearly having
been used as a footpath by someone.

00:09:45.670 --> 00:09:46.670
But who?

00:09:46.670 --> 00:09:51.060
Well, on April 12, 1993, the Foundation got
their answer.

00:09:51.060 --> 00:09:56.530
SCP-8048's bulkhead opened, and a man stepped
out, snapping his fingers and promptly sealing

00:09:56.530 --> 00:09:57.959
the door behind him.

00:09:57.959 --> 00:10:00.779
He was designated PoI-8048.

00:10:00.779 --> 00:10:06.000
He was a 32-year-old man of French Canadian
descent, answering to the name of Dr. Laurence

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:07.000
Michaud.

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:11.010
He made a series of claims that the Foundation
found dubious, but noted in the official file

00:10:11.010 --> 00:10:12.820
for SCP-8048 just the same.

00:10:12.820 --> 00:10:16.240
These included, but were not limited to:

00:10:16.240 --> 00:10:18.680
"SCP-8048 is a time machine.

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:24.140
He held the office of O5-11 in the year 3030
from an alternate timeline.

00:10:24.140 --> 00:10:30.220
Said timeline experienced a "modified" ΩK-Class
End-of-Death scenario that coincided with

00:10:30.220 --> 00:10:34.260
the invasion of a Tiamat-class anomaly known
as SCP-UBU.

00:10:34.260 --> 00:10:41.290
SCP-UBU was an extremely dangerous and sadistic
entity who was capable of, among other things,

00:10:41.290 --> 00:10:45.880
neutralizing SCP-169 and SCP-682.

00:10:45.880 --> 00:10:50.310
His timeline's version of the Foundation launched
"Project Beluga," which resulted in an impossible

00:10:50.310 --> 00:10:55.250
war with SCP-UBU that lasted 441 years.

00:10:55.250 --> 00:11:02.690
PoI-8048 deliberately sabotaged SCP-319 to
act as a power source for SCP-8048, thus arriving

00:11:02.690 --> 00:11:06.870
in Lapland in the year 11,970 BCE.

00:11:06.870 --> 00:11:12.400
SCP-UBU will arrive in Greenland on May 12th,
2588.

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:17.270
PoI-8048 was able to extend his lifespan by
sharing his consciousness between a central

00:11:17.270 --> 00:11:24.279
computer within SCP-8048 and several thousand
bodies created by his personal hominid replicators.

00:11:24.279 --> 00:11:30.900
Said consciousness-sharing was achieved through
a book classified in the future as "SCP-YEZ."

00:11:30.900 --> 00:11:35.420
He wishes to assist the Foundation in the
termination of SCP-UBU, and has laid out a

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:38.870
plan for its termination as outlined in Document-8048-Zeta."

00:11:38.870 --> 00:11:44.420
There were, of course, concerns about the
man's legitimacy, but after Michaud mentioned

00:11:44.420 --> 00:11:49.959
over 104 specific terms and data points known
only to members of the O5 Council, the Foundation

00:11:49.959 --> 00:11:53.100
was forced to take him at least a little bit
seriously.

00:11:53.100 --> 00:11:57.790
A motion was filed, requesting that PoI-8048
be allowed to assist the Foundation with the

00:11:57.790 --> 00:12:00.839
termination of SCP-UBU as per Document-8048-Zeta.

00:12:00.839 --> 00:12:09.149
O5-4 voted Yea, O5-7 abstained, and the rest
of the council voted Nay.

00:12:09.149 --> 00:12:10.770
The motion failed to pass.

00:12:10.770 --> 00:12:15.649
A follow-up motion was filed in response,
requesting that PoI-8048 be allowed to assist

00:12:15.649 --> 00:12:19.990
the Foundation with their own strategy to
respond to SCP-UBU.

00:12:19.990 --> 00:12:26.020
O5-1, O5-4, O5-7, and O5-10 abstained from
voting.

00:12:26.020 --> 00:12:27.590
The rest voted Nay.

00:12:27.590 --> 00:12:29.459
The motion failed to pass.

00:12:29.459 --> 00:12:35.790
On April 14, 1995, Dr. Isaiah Henderson and
PoI-8048 sat down for an interview.

00:12:35.790 --> 00:12:39.811
When asked to state his name, Dr. Michaud
also recited a memetic passphrase that, when

00:12:39.811 --> 00:12:45.519
spoken by anyone other than an O5-11 of past
or present, would cause them to burst into

00:12:45.519 --> 00:12:46.519
flames.

00:12:46.519 --> 00:12:50.630
The two men were at odds from the beginning,
Dr. Michaud expressing dismay and frustration

00:12:50.630 --> 00:12:52.450
that his proposal was rejected.

00:12:52.450 --> 00:12:57.019
Meanwhile, Dr. Henderson countered with the
insistence that Michaud's proposed plan was

00:12:57.019 --> 00:13:00.880
rejected for posing an unnecessary risk to
the civilian public.

00:13:00.880 --> 00:13:06.160
They debated for a moment, before Dr. Henderson
announced the Foundation's next plan of action.

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:10.839
Dr. Michaud was to be terminated, and the
Foundation would proceed with its plans without

00:13:10.839 --> 00:13:11.839
him.

00:13:11.839 --> 00:13:14.400
At that point, Dr. Henderson terminated Michaud,
as ordered.

00:13:14.400 --> 00:13:20.030
He didn't count on one thing, though: Michaud
was no longer an ordinary man, bound to one

00:13:20.030 --> 00:13:21.030
body.

00:13:21.030 --> 00:13:25.960
He hopped into the body of a guard, then into
the body of O5-4, to deliver a vital message.

00:13:25.960 --> 00:13:31.320
He had started this plan alone, and he was
ready to bring it to a close alone.

00:13:31.320 --> 00:13:35.139
Project Beluga would continue, with or without
the Foundation's support.

00:13:35.139 --> 00:13:40.090
Dr. Michaud returned to the bulkhead, climbing
back inside and sealing it behind him.

00:13:40.090 --> 00:13:43.740
He had hoped to have the Foundation behind
him, had hoped they would be allies in the

00:13:43.740 --> 00:13:46.630
fight against the greatest evil mankind ever
encountered.

00:13:46.630 --> 00:13:48.149
But they disappointed him.

00:13:48.149 --> 00:13:52.710
He had waited thousands of years, only for
the organization he devoted his life to to

00:13:52.710 --> 00:13:53.960
try and kill him.

00:13:53.960 --> 00:13:57.040
Well, he wasn't going to go down without a
fight.

00:13:57.040 --> 00:14:00.010
This was bigger than the Foundation, bigger
than anyone.

00:14:00.010 --> 00:14:04.540
And no living person was as equipped to handle
UBU as he was.

00:14:04.540 --> 00:14:08.670
So, he resumed Project Beluga, as a one-man
operation.

00:14:08.670 --> 00:14:11.600
He issued a mission statement, which read
as follows:

00:14:11.600 --> 00:14:18.740
"On May 12th, 2588, the entity known as SCP-UBU
invaded and pillaged human civilization for

00:14:18.740 --> 00:14:22.730
no other motivation than cruelty and selfish
gratification.

00:14:22.730 --> 00:14:28.079
Shortly thereafter, Project Beluga was founded
as a joint effort between the Global Occult

00:14:28.079 --> 00:14:33.089
Coalition and the SCP Foundation for the purposes
of UBU's destruction.

00:14:33.089 --> 00:14:35.610
UBU is not merely a threat to human safety.

00:14:35.610 --> 00:14:40.930
He is an affront to every positive and loving
concept in the human consciousness.

00:14:40.930 --> 00:14:46.839
Rather than our lives, he seeks to destroy
our quality of life to sate his own sick desires.

00:14:46.839 --> 00:14:49.080
Think about it: The taste of ice cream.

00:14:49.080 --> 00:14:50.209
Playing with your dog.

00:14:50.209 --> 00:14:52.660
The way you felt after your first kiss.

00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:54.880
That is UBU's sworn enemy.

00:14:54.880 --> 00:14:56.829
No fate is too cruel for him.

00:14:56.829 --> 00:14:58.820
No hatred is strong enough.

00:14:58.820 --> 00:15:03.660
When Project Beluga's charter was signed,
592 GOC officers and Foundation staff were

00:15:03.660 --> 00:15:05.050
present at the ceremony.

00:15:05.050 --> 00:15:08.100
Our troops numbered in the hundreds of thousands.

00:15:08.100 --> 00:15:13.410
I, Dr. Laurence Michaud, am the only surviving
member - and always will be.

00:15:13.410 --> 00:15:19.640
What I lack in numbers is compensated thousandfold
by my weapons, my mind, my replicated bodies,

00:15:19.640 --> 00:15:21.329
and eons of experience.

00:15:21.329 --> 00:15:27.470
The following record serves one purpose alone:
that once justice has been brought to UBU,

00:15:27.470 --> 00:15:32.819
humans in the shining and golden UBU-free
future will understand that one person can

00:15:32.819 --> 00:15:38.579
accomplish through the power of hard science
and raw emotion entwined in a perfect and

00:15:38.579 --> 00:15:43.199
indestructible braid. …and while we're at
it, you're very welcome."

00:15:43.199 --> 00:15:47.130
Over the next several hundred years, Michaud
worked to secure ownership of Kangaatsiaq,

00:15:47.130 --> 00:15:49.810
Greenland, through a Project Beluga civilian
front.

00:15:49.810 --> 00:15:54.470
He evacuated the civilian population from
the area, then spent a century constructing

00:15:54.470 --> 00:15:55.860
a superweapon.

00:15:55.860 --> 00:16:02.579
With 100 high-yield nuclear weapons, heat-amplification
runes, a targeting beacon for SCP-DAG, and

00:16:02.579 --> 00:16:09.070
five antimatter-gathering pods from SCP-HNM
in place, he was finally ready for UBU to

00:16:09.070 --> 00:16:10.420
manifest again.

00:16:10.420 --> 00:16:17.010
Now check out “The O5 Council Must Die SCP-001
- The Way It Ends - Ouroboros Cycle” and

00:16:17.010 --> 00:16:20.139
“Insane SCP-001 Fight - Gate Guardian VS
Scarlet King!”

